<title>UK: UK drug stocks down in Roche rumour switch.</title>
<headline>UK drug stocks down in Roche rumour switch.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in SmithKline Beecham Plc and Zeneca Group Plc fell back in late trading on Friday as speculation about a Roche Holding AG takeover bid switched to the U.S, analysts said on Friday.</p>
<p>One analyst, who asked not to be named, said shares in the two British groups had slipped back on rumours that Roche was looking at the U.S. company Warner-Lamber Co.  </p>
<p>Shares in SmithKline Beecham were down 16 1/2 pence at 863 1/2 shortly before the close, well below a high of 890 pence. Zeneca was down 37 pence at 1686 1/2.</p>
<p>Both shares gained on Thursday, partly because of falls in the value of sterling.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Birt London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
